{"chunk_id": "8e2ac8a682a7", "text": "A grand martial exhibition is held to display the skills of the Kuru princes before the kingdom. Kings, nobles, and citizens gather around a magnificent arena as Drona presides over the tournament. One by one the princes demonstrate their mastery of weapons\u2014archery, chariot driving, swordplay\u2014astonishing the crowd. The tension rises when Bhima and Duryodhana enter the arena with maces, their rivalry stirring the spectators into divided factions until Ashwatthaman restrains them. Drona then dramatically presents Arjuna, his most beloved pupil. Arjuna appears in radiant armor and displays his prowess, causing the assembly to erupt in praise. Kunti is moved to tears at the acclaim for her son, while Dhritarashtra, hearing the uproar, asks the reason and is told that Arjuna has entered the arena. The scene elevates Arjuna as the foremost warrior and foreshadows the rivalries that will shape the epic.\nAt the princes\u2019 martial exhibition, Bhima and Duryodhana nearly fight before Drona halts them and presents Arjuna, whose dazzling skill electrifies the crowd.\nThemes: martial exhibition, rivalry, teacher's pride, public acclaim, heroic introduction", "vector": [-0.012094548903405666, -0.01816852204501629, -0.008530260995030403, 0.004672287032008171, -0.012014452368021011, 0.021852953359484673, -0.024963362142443657, 0.0009686652338132262, -0.023388134315609932, -0.02349492907524109, 0.00419504614546895, 0.00774932187050581, -0.0003696112835314125, 0.013950114138424397, -0.002107535256072879, 0.003544263541698456, 0.03898022323846817, -0.009951971471309662, 0.009891899302601814, -0.0264584943652153, -0.004996009636670351, -0.01424380112439394, 0.0010187254520133138, 0.010299055837094784, -0.015685535967350006, 0.02672548219561577, 0.014577535912394524, -0.02928856573998928, 0.006401033140718937, -0.0072754183784127235, -0.008530260995030403, 0.008243249729275703, 0.017407607287168503, -0.008944092318415642, -0.0159525237